1
00:01:00,840 --> 00:01:02,120
<i>Runch, if your happiness</i>

2
00:01:02,200 --> 00:01:04,200
<i>comes at the cost of treating me horribly,</i>

3
00:01:04,280 --> 00:01:08,200
I won't back down. There's no way
I'm losing you to that girl.

4
00:01:08,280 --> 00:01:12,640
<i>Today's event feels so sweet and warm,</i>
<i>as if it was a family party.</i>

5
00:01:12,720 --> 00:01:14,400
They humiliated you,

6
00:01:14,480 --> 00:01:16,560
<i>so you've got to do the same.</i>

7
00:01:19,160 --> 00:01:20,200
Stop it, Mom!

8
00:01:20,280 --> 00:01:21,480
What the hell are you doing?!

9
00:01:22,880 --> 00:01:26,080
That old hag needs to learn
that she can't just slap anyone.

10
00:01:26,160 --> 00:01:27,640
Come on, then, you little brat!

11
00:01:27,720 --> 00:01:29,040
- That's enough, Mom!
- Come on.

12
00:01:34,920 --> 00:01:37,480
I never imagined
you'd go this far to hurt me.

13
00:01:38,000 --> 00:01:39,680
I never imagined

14
00:01:39,760 --> 00:01:42,280
you'd go this far to hurt my wife either.

15
00:01:43,000 --> 00:01:44,800
I'm just standing up for myself.

16
00:01:44,880 --> 00:01:46,040
If I don't fight,

17
00:01:46,120 --> 00:01:48,200
I'll be left with nothing.

18
00:01:49,240 --> 00:01:51,200
You weren't standing up for yourself.

19
00:01:51,280 --> 00:01:53,040
All you did was hurt someone

20
00:01:53,120 --> 00:01:55,040
and call it love.

21
00:01:57,120 --> 00:01:58,680
I only drove you back here

22
00:02:00,000 --> 00:02:01,720
because you're still my mother.

23
00:02:03,280 --> 00:02:04,760
But from now on,

24
00:02:04,840 --> 00:02:07,840
I won't take responsibility
for your actions anymore.

25
00:02:08,440 --> 00:02:10,280
What actions? I'm not scared.

26
00:02:12,640 --> 00:02:14,240
Well, I sure hope so.

27
00:02:15,120 --> 00:02:17,520
Because Neen definitely
won't let you get away with this.

28
00:02:20,600 --> 00:02:21,920
What's that supposed to mean?

29
00:02:25,440 --> 00:02:27,400
You attacked her today.

30
00:02:27,480 --> 00:02:29,600
There were witnesses and videos.

31
00:02:29,680 --> 00:02:31,320
The evidence is clear.

32
00:02:33,360 --> 00:02:34,920
Neen's not the quiet type,

33
00:02:35,480 --> 00:02:37,200
and she's no pushover.

34
00:02:37,800 --> 00:02:41,720
She's been putting up with you
out of respect for me.

35
00:02:41,800 --> 00:02:43,840
But what you did today

36
00:02:43,920 --> 00:02:46,640
was totally inhumane.

37
00:02:48,080 --> 00:02:49,440
In that case,

38
00:02:49,520 --> 00:02:51,560
I have nothing to lose now.

39
00:02:53,120 --> 00:02:54,440
I see you've made your choice.

40
00:03:23,840 --> 00:03:24,920
Neen,

41
00:03:25,520 --> 00:03:28,480
- can I go say hi to your parents?
- Don't.

42
00:03:40,240 --> 00:03:42,120
Let me talk to them first.

43
00:03:44,040 --> 00:03:45,240
You should go home.

44
00:03:53,080 --> 00:03:55,280
Then, feel free to call me…

45
00:03:57,120 --> 00:03:59,520
whenever you want to come home.

46
00:04:04,400 --> 00:04:05,480
Sure.

47
00:04:08,040 --> 00:04:09,160
You should get going.

48
00:04:45,960 --> 00:04:48,240
Yes, please take care of it for me.

49
00:04:49,400 --> 00:04:50,480
Thank you.

50
00:04:53,600 --> 00:04:55,480
I called the restaurant

51
00:04:55,560 --> 00:04:58,480
to ask everyone
who filmed the incident today

52
00:04:58,560 --> 00:05:00,280
not to publish the videos.

53
00:05:01,200 --> 00:05:03,960
They said they’d do their best to help.

54
00:05:06,040 --> 00:05:09,840
Do you want to go up and get some rest,
or should we put a cold pack on your face?

55
00:05:10,360 --> 00:05:12,600
We'll figure out what to do tomorrow.

56
00:05:16,840 --> 00:05:19,640
Take it easy and get some rest.

57
00:05:20,320 --> 00:05:23,920
As for the rest,
let me handle everything for you.

58
00:05:28,880 --> 00:05:30,080
Nai,

59
00:05:31,640 --> 00:05:33,720
please don't blame Runch for this.

60
00:05:35,480 --> 00:05:37,880
Mom and Dad want to blame her too.

61
00:05:38,640 --> 00:05:39,840
It's not just me.

62
00:05:40,560 --> 00:05:41,720
Then…

63
00:05:44,560 --> 00:05:47,360
can you two not blame her for this?

64
00:05:51,720 --> 00:05:53,160
I won't.

65
00:05:56,040 --> 00:05:57,720
I want you

66
00:05:58,440 --> 00:05:59,600
to divorce her.

67
00:06:04,520 --> 00:06:05,560
Honey…

68
00:06:09,760 --> 00:06:11,680
That's all I ask.

69
00:06:13,360 --> 00:06:14,600
Neen.

70
00:06:15,320 --> 00:06:17,200
We all love you.

71
00:06:22,040 --> 00:06:24,160
I've always taken good care of you.

72
00:06:24,920 --> 00:06:26,440
I can't stand

73
00:06:27,960 --> 00:06:30,040
seeing you get treated this way.

74
00:06:40,760 --> 00:06:44,560
I'm sorry for troubling you all.

75
00:06:49,560 --> 00:06:50,600
Neen,

76
00:06:51,440 --> 00:06:53,040
there's no need to apologize.

77
00:06:54,160 --> 00:06:55,520
You didn't do anything wrong.

78
00:07:01,720 --> 00:07:04,200
Look, I'm not forcing you.

79
00:07:05,800 --> 00:07:07,760
I want you to think it over.

80
00:07:09,560 --> 00:07:11,320
There might be a way

81
00:07:11,400 --> 00:07:13,480
to prevent Mrs. Ging
from doing this again.

82
00:07:18,200 --> 00:07:20,600
No matter what it takes,

83
00:07:20,680 --> 00:07:21,840
I'll try every way.

84
00:07:54,360 --> 00:07:56,200
When no one was around to trouble you,

85
00:07:56,280 --> 00:07:58,600
you were doing just fine, weren't you?

86
00:08:00,800 --> 00:08:01,800
Yeah.

87
00:08:08,640 --> 00:08:10,240
It was like a dream.

88
00:08:13,640 --> 00:08:16,840
It felt just like
when we were newly married.

89
00:08:23,360 --> 00:08:25,040
But it was just a dream.

90
00:08:27,400 --> 00:08:30,080
In the end,
I had to wake up and face reality.

91
00:08:33,840 --> 00:08:36,640
Nai and your dad
are taking this very seriously,

92
00:08:36,720 --> 00:08:38,400
so I'm sure she'll fold.

93
00:08:39,080 --> 00:08:41,520
Then, you can go back to being happy.

94
00:08:41,600 --> 00:08:44,880
But Runch has to let us
deal with that troublemaker.

95
00:08:44,960 --> 00:08:47,320
She will. She'll let us do anything.

96
00:08:48,000 --> 00:08:50,320
But Runch can't be truly happy

97
00:08:50,400 --> 00:08:53,080
if her parents are still in a tight spot.

98
00:08:57,720 --> 00:08:58,960
I understand.

99
00:09:02,080 --> 00:09:03,560
I mean…

100
00:09:04,960 --> 00:09:06,480
I just feel like

101
00:09:06,560 --> 00:09:10,080
there's no way for me and Runch
to be happy together.

102
00:09:18,720 --> 00:09:20,640
Maybe we should break up.

103
00:09:22,520 --> 00:09:23,600
Neen!

104
00:09:25,680 --> 00:09:27,160
Are you sure about that?

105
00:09:28,160 --> 00:09:29,160
Hmm?

106
00:09:32,240 --> 00:09:33,720
I don't know.

107
00:09:36,680 --> 00:09:40,200
I don't know anything. I'm just so tired.

108
00:09:43,840 --> 00:09:45,840
It's okay, honey.

109
00:09:45,920 --> 00:09:47,960
I really am.

110
00:09:48,040 --> 00:09:48,960
It's okay.

111
00:09:50,040 --> 00:09:51,680
There's no need to think yet.

112
00:09:52,320 --> 00:09:54,440
Okay, honey? Just get some rest.

113
00:10:00,800 --> 00:10:02,120
Easy now.

114
00:10:14,160 --> 00:10:17,040
MOTHER-IN-LAW IN HEATED FIGHT
WITH RICH DAUGHTER-IN-LAW

115
00:10:18,800 --> 00:10:20,920
<i>You shameless bitch.</i>
<i>You always act all nice</i>

116
00:10:21,000 --> 00:10:23,960
<i>and sweet, but you're just a selfish girl</i>

117
00:10:24,040 --> 00:10:25,560
<i>who wants to steal everything from others!</i>

118
00:10:26,840 --> 00:10:28,320
<i>If that's how you feel…</i>

119
00:10:28,400 --> 00:10:30,400
- Nai, what's that?
<i>- …then that's your problem, not mine.</i>

120
00:10:30,480 --> 00:10:31,440
<i>You crazy bitch!</i>

121
00:10:33,400 --> 00:10:34,600
Why the long face?

122
00:10:35,640 --> 00:10:36,880
Is something wrong?

123
00:10:38,600 --> 00:10:41,720
The videos from the restaurant
are being shared all over the internet.

124
00:10:44,200 --> 00:10:45,320
What?

125
00:10:45,400 --> 00:10:47,440
You said it was all under control.

126
00:10:47,520 --> 00:10:48,520
So, how come…?

127
00:10:53,400 --> 00:10:55,200
It'll be easy to find out who posted them.

128
00:11:03,080 --> 00:11:04,400
Hey, Utt.

129
00:11:04,480 --> 00:11:07,520
Did you hear? Our boss's mother
hit her daughter-in-law at a restaurant.

130
00:11:07,600 --> 00:11:08,880
It's crazy!

131
00:11:08,960 --> 00:11:11,120
Of course I did.
That's why I'm in a good mood.

132
00:11:12,680 --> 00:11:13,720
Utt,

133
00:11:13,800 --> 00:11:16,080
Mr. Apichet wants to see you now.

134
00:11:22,720 --> 00:11:24,800
You wanted to speak to me, Mr. Apichet?

135
00:11:37,360 --> 00:11:38,720
Surprised to see me?

136
00:11:43,360 --> 00:11:44,400
What do you want?

137
00:11:52,960 --> 00:11:54,240
You're fired, Utt.

138
00:11:56,240 --> 00:11:57,600
Fired?

139
00:11:57,680 --> 00:12:00,240
On what grounds? What did I do wrong?

140
00:12:02,000 --> 00:12:03,400
You seriously don't know?

141
00:12:11,200 --> 00:12:12,680
I know you did this.

142
00:12:16,800 --> 00:12:18,480
Do you have proof?

143
00:12:19,520 --> 00:12:21,680
If I didn't,
I wouldn't be saying all this.

144
00:12:23,520 --> 00:12:25,320
You have 30 minutes.

145
00:12:25,920 --> 00:12:27,800
Go pack up your things.

146
00:12:30,760 --> 00:12:32,360
Don't make me do this the hard way.

147
00:12:39,440 --> 00:12:43,040
You're going to regret your decision.

148
00:13:12,920 --> 00:13:13,840
Are you happy now?

149
00:13:15,320 --> 00:13:17,080
You got your case and the credit too.

150
00:13:17,720 --> 00:13:19,000
You won.

151
00:13:19,880 --> 00:13:21,280
You getting fired

152
00:13:21,360 --> 00:13:23,240
- had nothing to do with me.
- Yes, it did!

153
00:13:23,840 --> 00:13:25,040
If it weren't for you,

154
00:13:25,560 --> 00:13:27,040
this wouldn't have happened to me.

155
00:13:28,960 --> 00:13:30,640
You act all nice,

156
00:13:31,480 --> 00:13:33,000
as if you're the victim.

157
00:13:33,520 --> 00:13:35,880
But really,
I'm the victim you're trampling on!

158
00:13:36,600 --> 00:13:40,160
You brought this on yourself. All of it.

159
00:13:40,240 --> 00:13:43,000
So now you have to face the consequences.

160
00:13:43,680 --> 00:13:45,440
Screw you!

161
00:13:45,520 --> 00:13:47,560
I hope you're never happy.

162
00:13:47,640 --> 00:13:49,680
That you'll be alone
for the rest of your life.

163
00:14:13,680 --> 00:14:16,360
She hasn't said anything
since this morning.

164
00:14:23,360 --> 00:14:25,720
Maybe she's just figuring out

165
00:14:26,600 --> 00:14:28,240
what to do next.

166
00:14:32,000 --> 00:14:33,840
I'm just worried

167
00:14:33,920 --> 00:14:37,120
that she'll force herself to stay
so she doesn't lose anyone.

168
00:14:38,600 --> 00:14:40,400
What would you do if you were her?

169
00:14:43,560 --> 00:14:45,320
I just want her to be safe.

170
00:14:45,880 --> 00:14:48,400
Nothing matters more than that.

171
00:14:50,640 --> 00:14:52,560
This isn't Runch's fault, though.

172
00:14:52,640 --> 00:14:54,440
She loves our daughter too.

173
00:14:56,600 --> 00:14:57,880
You're right.

174
00:15:00,440 --> 00:15:03,440
But love alone won't fix anything.

175
00:15:11,520 --> 00:15:14,080
I wonder how she'll go about this.

176
00:15:20,720 --> 00:15:22,600
Whatever she decides,

177
00:15:23,960 --> 00:15:25,560
as her parents,

178
00:15:26,600 --> 00:15:29,200
we'll always welcome her back.

179
00:16:20,960 --> 00:16:22,080
Runch,

180
00:16:23,000 --> 00:16:24,360
did you see that shooting star?

181
00:16:26,560 --> 00:16:27,680
An actual shooting star--

182
00:16:50,120 --> 00:16:52,800
NEW MESSAGE FROM RUNCH

183
00:16:52,880 --> 00:16:55,080
<i>Did you eat yet?</i>

184
00:17:07,920 --> 00:17:09,040
NEEN

185
00:17:09,119 --> 00:17:12,599
<i>Not yet. What about you?</i>

186
00:17:15,839 --> 00:17:17,440
<i>I can't eat.</i>

187
00:17:17,520 --> 00:17:20,960
<i>I miss you too much.</i>
<i>I want you to come home.</i>

188
00:17:31,520 --> 00:17:33,720
<i>Please give me some more time, Runch.</i>

189
00:17:42,480 --> 00:17:46,680
<i>Okay, I understand. I can wait.</i>

190
00:17:46,760 --> 00:17:49,000
<i>No matter how long it takes,</i>
<i>I'll wait for you.</i>

191
00:21:05,520 --> 00:21:07,680
- Oh. Have a seat, honey.
- Neen.

192
00:21:07,760 --> 00:21:08,880
Come sit with us.

193
00:21:08,960 --> 00:21:10,160
Come on.

194
00:21:18,680 --> 00:21:21,920
This is Mr. Chuchai.
He is our company's lawyer.

195
00:21:23,120 --> 00:21:24,120
Good afternoon.

196
00:21:27,320 --> 00:21:28,680
I called him here

197
00:21:29,320 --> 00:21:31,600
so we can file a lawsuit
against Mrs. Gingkamol

198
00:21:31,680 --> 00:21:33,240
for assaulting you.

199
00:21:35,480 --> 00:21:36,400
A lawsuit?

200
00:21:40,120 --> 00:21:42,640
We can't let this slide.

201
00:21:42,720 --> 00:21:44,760
This time, it's not just a family matter.

202
00:21:46,280 --> 00:21:49,360
But, Dad, I don't want to sue her yet.

203
00:21:51,480 --> 00:21:52,600
Why not?

204
00:21:53,640 --> 00:21:56,080
We have evidence,
and she left visible marks on you.

205
00:21:56,160 --> 00:21:57,440
Why wouldn't you sue her?

206
00:21:58,720 --> 00:22:00,640
I didn't say I wouldn't.

207
00:22:01,360 --> 00:22:03,120
I'm just not ready yet.

208
00:22:03,680 --> 00:22:05,520
Can you give me some time?

209
00:22:06,400 --> 00:22:07,960
For what?

210
00:22:08,880 --> 00:22:10,960
For her to act this way again?

211
00:22:14,560 --> 00:22:16,280
I don't want you to live in fear

212
00:22:16,880 --> 00:22:18,760
and mistake it for patience.

213
00:22:21,520 --> 00:22:23,360
I know that, Dad.

214
00:22:23,440 --> 00:22:26,240
I just don't want things to escalate.

215
00:22:29,000 --> 00:22:30,880
I'm doing this to protect you.

216
00:22:35,240 --> 00:22:36,560
I know.

217
00:22:38,880 --> 00:22:42,400
But right now, I need some time
to process my emotions.

218
00:22:54,080 --> 00:22:55,840
- Neen.
- Honey. It's okay.

219
00:22:55,920 --> 00:22:57,320
I'll talk to her.

220
00:22:57,880 --> 00:22:58,880
Okay?

221
00:23:16,400 --> 00:23:17,800
Neen.

222
00:23:17,880 --> 00:23:20,440
Would you mind if I asked you something?

223
00:23:25,320 --> 00:23:27,600
Why won't you sue Mrs. Gingkamol?

224
00:23:33,320 --> 00:23:35,440
I'm not worried about the case.

225
00:23:37,640 --> 00:23:39,440
I'm worried about its consequences.

226
00:23:40,520 --> 00:23:42,000
Consequences for whom?

227
00:23:47,280 --> 00:23:48,400
For Runch.

228
00:23:58,160 --> 00:23:59,440
You see…

229
00:24:00,640 --> 00:24:02,560
if this continues,

230
00:24:02,640 --> 00:24:04,600
no matter what the verdict is,

231
00:24:05,280 --> 00:24:08,920
I'll be fine, but Runch will be crushed.

232
00:24:09,000 --> 00:24:11,640
After all, the culprit is her own mother.

233
00:24:13,080 --> 00:24:16,800
Her mother may be horrible and violent,

234
00:24:17,640 --> 00:24:20,640
but in the end, it's her who'll carry
the guilt for the rest of her life.

235
00:24:24,920 --> 00:24:29,400
I don't want to make her choose between
justice and being a good daughter

236
00:24:31,040 --> 00:24:34,520
even though she said
I could do whatever I want to her mother.

237
00:24:36,280 --> 00:24:39,240
What about you?
Who will make the choice for you?

238
00:24:43,160 --> 00:24:44,800
I am making that choice.

239
00:24:47,560 --> 00:24:50,960
Your dad and I never wanted you
to endure anything for anyone.

240
00:24:52,680 --> 00:24:54,000
I'm not.

241
00:24:56,280 --> 00:24:57,800
I just…

242
00:24:57,880 --> 00:25:00,960
want to do one last thing for Runch.

243
00:25:01,040 --> 00:25:02,720
Because on the day it happened,

244
00:25:03,240 --> 00:25:07,080
she defended me,
and her mother hit her too.

245
00:25:16,920 --> 00:25:18,800
I feel like…

246
00:25:22,440 --> 00:25:24,680
when she's with me…

247
00:25:27,240 --> 00:25:29,200
she seems miserable.

248
00:25:36,240 --> 00:25:38,080
What do you mean?

249
00:25:44,480 --> 00:25:45,680
I…

250
00:25:47,920 --> 00:25:49,960
I just want her to know that

251
00:25:51,480 --> 00:25:53,040
I may be hurt,

252
00:25:54,000 --> 00:25:57,520
but I won't let that ruin her life.

253
00:26:01,920 --> 00:26:05,520
I don't want her last memory of us

254
00:26:07,280 --> 00:26:10,320
to be me suing her mother.

255
00:26:13,280 --> 00:26:15,880
You're way too nice, Neen.

256
00:26:17,760 --> 00:26:19,880
I don't want to be nice.

257
00:26:21,040 --> 00:26:25,000
I just want us to break up
without hating each other.

258
00:26:32,400 --> 00:26:35,720
I don't know if you're making
the right decision,

259
00:26:36,880 --> 00:26:38,440
but I do know

260
00:26:40,040 --> 00:26:41,680
that it must be difficult for you.

261
00:26:53,360 --> 00:26:55,600
I still love her, Mom.

262
00:27:00,400 --> 00:27:02,720
I want to see her happy.

263
00:27:03,800 --> 00:27:07,880
It may be rough for a while
after we break up,

264
00:27:09,280 --> 00:27:10,200
but…

265
00:27:12,120 --> 00:27:14,520
if she can get through it,

266
00:27:16,640 --> 00:27:20,080
she might be happier
than when she's with me.

267
00:27:24,920 --> 00:27:26,080
Aw, honey…

268
00:28:03,080 --> 00:28:07,600
YOU HAVE A NEW MESSAGE

269
00:28:12,080 --> 00:28:14,160
<i>Let's meet at home this evening.</i>

270
00:28:23,160 --> 00:28:25,960
Have a seat. The food's still warm.

271
00:28:39,840 --> 00:28:41,960
These are from your restaurant.

272
00:28:43,080 --> 00:28:45,200
Is there a special occasion?

273
00:28:48,360 --> 00:28:49,480
No.

274
00:28:50,240 --> 00:28:52,440
I just wanted you to eat what you like.

275
00:28:54,640 --> 00:28:57,120
You really shouldn't have.

276
00:28:59,280 --> 00:29:01,480
Eat it while it's hot.

277
00:29:13,040 --> 00:29:14,320
You know,

278
00:29:15,920 --> 00:29:19,120
I remember all your likes and dislikes.

279
00:29:21,360 --> 00:29:23,720
I can even remember the day we first met

280
00:29:24,400 --> 00:29:26,040
three years ago.

281
00:29:29,160 --> 00:29:30,840
I remember too.

282
00:29:31,840 --> 00:29:33,840
We first met

283
00:29:34,720 --> 00:29:37,120
in the restroom at a coffee shop.

284
00:29:39,440 --> 00:29:41,640
You spilled coffee all over yourself.

285
00:29:42,920 --> 00:29:45,560
So you gave me a change of clothes,

286
00:29:46,080 --> 00:29:48,120
and we exchanged contact details.

287
00:29:51,720 --> 00:29:55,800
You know, I fell in love with you
the moment I saw you.

288
00:29:58,760 --> 00:30:01,360
I fell in love with your beauty

289
00:30:01,960 --> 00:30:03,560
and your smile.

290
00:30:08,360 --> 00:30:09,560
My heart

291
00:30:09,640 --> 00:30:12,600
beat so fast, it felt like it was
going to burst out of my chest.

292
00:30:14,880 --> 00:30:16,720
Me too.

293
00:30:17,920 --> 00:30:20,120
Your smile

294
00:30:20,200 --> 00:30:22,080
and your cheerful vibe

295
00:30:22,640 --> 00:30:25,320
got me dreaming every night

296
00:30:26,400 --> 00:30:28,600
that I'd get to see you every day.

297
00:30:36,040 --> 00:30:38,560
And then, that dream came true.

298
00:30:45,120 --> 00:30:47,160
We got married,

299
00:30:47,840 --> 00:30:49,320
and now we're living together.

300
00:30:55,440 --> 00:30:57,320
We get to see
each other's faces every day.

301
00:31:02,120 --> 00:31:03,880
I love you, Neen.

302
00:31:12,440 --> 00:31:14,440
I love you so much.

303
00:31:21,280 --> 00:31:22,960
I love you too.

304
00:31:28,280 --> 00:31:29,560
I love you the most.

305
00:31:41,280 --> 00:31:42,520
Runch.

306
00:31:50,880 --> 00:31:52,040
Yes?

307
00:32:02,480 --> 00:32:04,000
I want a divorce.

308
00:32:35,320 --> 00:32:36,720
Thank you

309
00:32:37,360 --> 00:32:39,720
for trying everything.

310
00:32:44,080 --> 00:32:46,160
I always knew

311
00:32:46,240 --> 00:32:49,640
you didn't want
any of those terrible things to happen.

312
00:32:50,520 --> 00:32:52,440
You had nothing to do with them.

313
00:33:07,280 --> 00:33:09,840
And I know

314
00:33:09,920 --> 00:33:13,440
you've been trying to save our marriage.

315
00:33:23,240 --> 00:33:24,760
Whatever you're thinking

316
00:33:26,440 --> 00:33:28,400
or feeling right now…

317
00:33:30,520 --> 00:33:32,000
can you tell me about it?

318
00:33:36,760 --> 00:33:38,200
I just

319
00:33:38,280 --> 00:33:41,880
don't want my love
to keep hurting you anymore.

320
00:33:44,360 --> 00:33:45,440
That's not true.

321
00:33:46,200 --> 00:33:47,440
It never did.

322
00:33:49,640 --> 00:33:52,720
Your love never hurt me, Neen.

323
00:33:55,680 --> 00:33:57,320
Runch, It's time to stop.

324
00:34:00,480 --> 00:34:02,520
You need to accept

325
00:34:02,600 --> 00:34:05,000
that no matter how hard we try,

326
00:34:05,080 --> 00:34:07,800
we can't escape
from the shadow of your mother.

327
00:34:13,320 --> 00:34:15,840
I'll give your mother what she wants.

328
00:34:17,679 --> 00:34:20,600
You can go back to being her daughter now.

329
00:34:22,120 --> 00:34:24,920
Let me do this one last thing for you.

330
00:34:55,920 --> 00:34:58,160
No matter what I say right now…

331
00:35:02,360 --> 00:35:05,080
I can't change your mind, can I?

332
00:35:10,400 --> 00:35:11,680
No.

333
00:35:19,480 --> 00:35:20,480
Okay.

334
00:35:28,080 --> 00:35:29,440
I understand now.

335
00:35:33,680 --> 00:35:35,120
Thank you

336
00:35:37,880 --> 00:35:40,240
for putting up with all of it for me.

337
00:36:13,000 --> 00:36:13,960
Neen!

338
00:36:16,960 --> 00:36:18,080
Neen!

339
00:36:24,320 --> 00:36:25,360
Neen!

340
00:36:26,880 --> 00:36:27,840
Neen!

341
00:36:29,320 --> 00:36:30,360
Neen.

342
00:36:35,280 --> 00:36:36,200
Yes?

343
00:36:38,240 --> 00:36:39,800
Where were you?

344
00:36:40,760 --> 00:36:43,200
I came downstairs to make you breakfast.

345
00:36:46,440 --> 00:36:47,960
Are you okay?

346
00:36:50,040 --> 00:36:52,480
I thought you'd leave me.

347
00:36:57,560 --> 00:36:59,240
I'll always be with you

348
00:37:00,080 --> 00:37:01,400
right there in your heart.

349
00:37:07,480 --> 00:37:08,320
Neen!

350
00:37:12,640 --> 00:37:13,880
Neen?

351
00:37:50,520 --> 00:37:51,720
Neen…

352
00:37:55,240 --> 00:37:56,400
Neen.

353
00:40:02,400 --> 00:40:03,440
Give me your hand.

354
00:40:03,520 --> 00:40:06,360
LAST YEAR

355
00:40:08,080 --> 00:40:11,360
Hold my hand and run along with me.

356
00:40:12,200 --> 00:40:14,560
I will never let go of your hand.

357
00:40:40,320 --> 00:40:43,520
Come to think of it,
relationships are pretty scary.

358
00:40:48,040 --> 00:40:49,960
What will you do

359
00:40:50,560 --> 00:40:51,640
if I get scared one day?

360
00:40:53,840 --> 00:40:57,120
I'll hold your hand like this…

361
00:41:00,200 --> 00:41:02,280
until you stop feeling scared.

362
00:41:11,000 --> 00:41:12,040
You promise?

363
00:41:18,160 --> 00:41:19,320
I promise.

364
00:41:33,000 --> 00:41:34,400
Here, put this on.

365
00:41:35,280 --> 00:41:36,640
It's windy.

366
00:41:36,720 --> 00:41:37,840
You'll catch a cold.

367
00:41:37,920 --> 00:41:39,040
Thank you.

368
00:41:41,720 --> 00:41:43,400
- Runch.
- Hmm?

369
00:41:45,080 --> 00:41:48,280
Can you be my happiness and mine alone?

370
00:41:48,920 --> 00:41:50,360
Of course.

371
00:41:50,440 --> 00:41:51,720
Forever.

372
00:42:09,760 --> 00:42:12,760
I want to take a picture for you.
You look so pretty today.

373
00:42:14,240 --> 00:42:15,320
Go for it.

374
00:42:23,560 --> 00:42:25,000
Don't look at the camera, though.

375
00:42:25,080 --> 00:42:26,880
Stare at the ocean

376
00:42:26,960 --> 00:42:29,360
as if you were thinking of something.

377
00:42:34,880 --> 00:42:36,240
Thinking of something?

378
00:42:36,320 --> 00:42:39,120
Can I think of you, then?

379
00:42:39,200 --> 00:42:40,480
Will the they turn out great?

380
00:42:42,160 --> 00:42:43,560
They are.

381
00:42:44,080 --> 00:42:46,240
They're so great

382
00:42:46,320 --> 00:42:48,120
that I'm getting distracted.

383
00:43:00,320 --> 00:43:01,200
Neen.

384
00:43:03,400 --> 00:43:06,320
You don't have to try to look sexy.

385
00:43:06,400 --> 00:43:07,720
You already caught my eye

386
00:43:07,800 --> 00:43:09,840
just with the way you are.

387
00:43:14,360 --> 00:43:15,320
Okay.

388
00:43:15,880 --> 00:43:17,680
Stunning.

389
00:43:18,280 --> 00:43:19,560
One, two, three.

390
00:43:21,240 --> 00:43:23,640
Got any good photos yet? Let me see.

391
00:43:25,040 --> 00:43:26,440
They're great.

392
00:43:26,520 --> 00:43:27,840
Here, let me show you.

393
00:43:28,880 --> 00:43:29,880
Aren't they great?

394
00:43:30,400 --> 00:43:31,720
Whoa!

395
00:43:31,800 --> 00:43:33,200
They're pretty great.

396
00:43:33,280 --> 00:43:34,360
Aren't they?

397
00:43:34,440 --> 00:43:35,880
I don't look like myself at all.

398
00:43:36,560 --> 00:43:39,920
I look like a whole different woman.

399
00:43:41,080 --> 00:43:42,760
No.

400
00:43:42,840 --> 00:43:44,400
It's still the same woman,

401
00:43:44,480 --> 00:43:47,520
but through the eyes
of someone who loves her.

402
00:43:49,160 --> 00:43:52,400
Then, can I be your model forever?

403
00:43:55,800 --> 00:43:57,320
Of course.

404
00:43:57,920 --> 00:43:59,360
Forever.

405
00:44:12,280 --> 00:44:14,400
Stop trying to control my life.

406
00:44:14,480 --> 00:44:16,880
And watch your life fall apart like this?

407
00:44:16,960 --> 00:44:19,720
My life isn't falling apart
because of Neen.

408
00:44:19,800 --> 00:44:22,960
If you still love Runch that much,
why divorce her?

409
00:44:23,040 --> 00:44:25,920
<i>Because she always sacrificed for me.</i>

410
00:44:35,320 --> 00:44:37,520
If the law can't punish someone like that,

411
00:44:37,600 --> 00:44:39,480
then we'll leave it to karma.

412
00:44:39,560 --> 00:44:41,080
You reap

413
00:44:41,160 --> 00:44:43,920
<i>what you sow.</i>

414
00:45:26,520 --> 00:45:28,920
Subtitle translation by:
Ramil Natnitiwitaya
